Description: Backport of typing._eval_type for older Python versions
 Like typing._eval_type, but lets older Python versions use newer
 typing features.
 .
 This package provides a Python 3 module that lets libraries which
 read type hints (such as Pydantic) support new-style typing syntax
 (e.g. X | Y unions) on Python versions older than 3.10, without
 requiring the from __future__ import annotations workaround.
